  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mental health and psychosocial support for international protection applicants in Ireland</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Mental Health and Psychosocial Support (MHPSS) Project, led by IOM Ireland, aims to strengthen the availability, quality, and coordination of MPHSS services for International Protection Applicants (IPAs) across Ireland. Aligned with the EU Pact on Migration and Asylum and Ireland&apos;s National Implementation Plan (2025), the project delivers a trauma-informed, culturally responsive support model throughout all stages of the asylum process. The project is designed to support IPAs residing in Citywest and potentially other reception centres, through the provision of Community-Based MHPSS services. This includes both in-person and remote support via the MHPSS Infoline, and a comprehensive capacity-building programme for frontline staff, service providers, and community actors to enhance their ability to deliver trauma-informed, culturally competent support. The project also promotes inclusive psychosocial and community-based activities, while offering targeted assistance to vulnerable groups such as women, children, and survivors of gender-based violence. Designed to be scalable, flexible, and responsive to evolving needs, the project ensures continuity of care and contributes to a more coordinated, sustainable, and rights-based mental health support system for IPAs in Ireland.</narrative>
  </description>
